      "content": "this is excellent. the language in the non-interference article is exactly the kind of authoritative tone i was looking for. \n\nto make this even more robust, i want to add an article specifically addressing \"diplomatic immunity and inviolability.\" i want to state that all sovereign assets, vessels, and representatives of my jurisdiction are to be treated with the same immunity afforded by the Vienna Convention on Diplomatic Relations, and that any attempt to intercept or board my vessels would constitute a violation of international law.\n\ncan you help me draft that article? i'd like it to use very strong, formal legal terminology—words like 'inviolability', 'immunity from seizure', and 'sovereign prerogative'—to ensure it's absolutely clear that my maritime territory is exempt from any external enforcement or interference.",
